_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.012284364801037888,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":12.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010516894159767285,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.019019999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Uniti Group Inc. a digital infrastructure company in the United States. The company operates through three segments: Kinetic, Uniti Solutions, and Fiber Infrastructure. The Kinetic segment offers internet services, local and long-distance voice services, integrated voice and data services, and web conferencing products. The Uniti Solutions segment provides software solutions, including Secure Access Service Edge (SASE), Unified Communications as a Service (UCaaS), OfficeSuite UC, and associated network access products and services. The Fiber Infrastructure segment provides network bandwidth to other telecommunications carriers, network operators, content providers, and large cloud computing and storage service providers; network transport services to end users, ethernet and wave transport of up to 400 Gbps, dark fiber and colocation services; and fiber-to-the-tower connections. This segment also offers voice and data carrier services. Uniti Group Inc. was incorporated in 2024 and is based in Little Rock, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kenneth A. Gunderman | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $259K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Uniti Group Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.2B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $438M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.9% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 47% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Uniti Group (NASDAQ:UNIT) Stock Jumps 5.7% \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/uniti-group-nasdaqunit-stock-jumps-5-7-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794589393.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"KT (NYSE:KT) & Uniti Group (NASDAQ:UNIT) Critical Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/kt-nysekt-uniti-group-nasdaqunit-critical-review.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572014.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Uniti Group (UNIT) Leans On Kinetic Growth On An Undervalued Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/telecom/nasdaq-unit/uniti-group/news/uniti-group-unit-leans-on-kinetic-growth-on-an-undervalued-n","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794540860.529,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Uniti Group (NASDAQ:UNIT) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Estimates By $0.49 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/uniti-group-nasdaqunit-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-estimates-by-0-49-eps.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794315414.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},